<title>Aortic Insufficiency: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0011-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>AI diagnosed on physical examination and&#x002F;or transthoracic echocardiogram</label>
<path target="cell-2"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Severe regurgitation?</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
<path target="cell-5">Indeterminate</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Symptoms due to regurgitation?</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
<path target="cell-8">Indeterminate</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-6">
<label>Aortic valve replacement</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Observation</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>Vasodilators?</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>CT or MRI, then reassess aortic diameter</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>LV echo findings: EF 55% or less, LVESD &gt;55 mm, LVEDD &gt;75 mm, or LVESI &gt;25 mm/m²?</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
<path target="cell-12">Indeterminate</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>Order cardiac catheterization or radionuclide angiography, then reassess LV findings</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Exercise testing, then reassess symptoms</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Ascending aorta diameter &gt;55–60 mm? (annuloaortic ectasia)</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-11">Indeterminate</path>
<path target="cell-10">No (moderate or severe AI)</path>
<path target="cell-9">No (mild AI)</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-5">
<label>Order transesophageal echocardiogram or aortic angiography, then reassess severity</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Data from Maurer G. Aortic regurgitation. <em>Heart</em> 2006;<strong>92</strong>:994&#x2013;1000;<xref ref="pubmed16775114" resource="acc029" /> and Bonow RO, Carabello BA, Chatterjee K, et al. ACC&#x002F;AGA 2006 guidelines for the management of patients with valvular heart disease. A report for the American College of Cardiology&#x002F;American Heart Association Task Force on Practice Guidelines. <em>Circulation</em> 2006;<strong>114</strong>:e84&#x2013;e231.<xref ref="pubmed16880336" resource="acc006" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
